            <profile id="045e-4ecf-7cab-8e48" name="Equipment and options (as printed in AoA2)" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">A Chieftain has a Hand weapon, light armour, thrusting or throwing spear, javelins and shield. Warband. Stealth. May ride a horse (+11) or a warhorse (+18) or a chariot as from the list below (+64). In each of these cases he becomes Ld7 but is no longer Warband.

A standard bearer has a hand weapon, light armour and shield. Army Standard Bearer. Warband. Stealth. May ride a horse (+11) or a warhorse (+18) or a chariot as from the list below (+64). In each of these cases he becomes Ld7 but is no longer Warband.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="7a88-affb-08a2-46f4" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">5+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
