  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="2a30-c0e0-2af9-a587" name="Gallic - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>Gallic (500 BC to 50 BC)

The Gauls spread through France, Switzerland, Austria, Britain, Italy, the Balkans and Asia Minor. This list covers those tribes present in France and Italy down to the conquest of Gaul by Julius Caesar. There is some debate over the density of Gallic warbands and while the list shows them as close order troops, you may if you wish field the warriors and fanatics in open order for +2 points per model.

ARMY COMPOSITION (as printed in AoA2):
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Cavalry and Chariots: up to 25%
  Skirmishers: up to 20%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%

ALLIES: A Gallic army may take allies from the Etruscan or Italian Hill Tribes lists.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
